			{
				"id": "about-it",
				"slug": "about",
				"locale": "it",
				"translationOf": "about",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "Chi sono",
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "it-about-1",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "it-about-1s",
									"text": "Ehi, grazie di essere passato di qui.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "it-about-2",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "it-about-2s",
									"text": "Sono Bryan. Questo sito e il posto in cui scrivo brevi note su quello che mi sta occupando la mente ultimamente. A volte sono citta e architettura. A volte foto fatte durante una camminata. A volte un libro, un disco, o una piccola osservazione che mi sembrava valesse la pena fermare.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "it-about-3",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "it-about-3s",
									"text": "Di lavoro faccio l'urbanista. Passo molto tempo a pensare a come funzionano i luoghi e a come potrebbero funzionare meglio. Trasporto pubblico, spazio pubblico, architettura e paesaggio finiscono spesso per entrare anche nel modo in cui guardo tutto il resto.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "it-about-4",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "it-about-4s",
									"text": "Fuori dal lavoro mi piace soprattutto fare cose. Scrivere, fotografare, coltivare, ascoltare musica, sperimentare in cucina, trafficare con piccoli siti personali. Internet una volta era pieno di siti personali piccoli e strani, e continuo a pensare che quella sia una delle sue forme migliori.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "it-about-5",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "it-about-5s",
									"text": "Sono cresciuto nella regione dei Grandi Laghi e ancora oggi mi manca moltissimo. Adesso vivo nel Pacific Northwest con la mia famiglia, dove tutto e piu verde, le foreste sono piene di muschio, e i pomodori nel mio giardino prendono un po' troppo spazio verso agosto.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "it-about-6",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "it-about-6s",
									"text": "Una parte del motivo per cui tengo in vita un sito cosi e che internet oggi puo sembrare piuttosto sgradevole ed estenuante. Volevo un piccolo angolo che risultasse piu personale e piu piacevole in cui tornare. Sto ancora lavorando per renderlo davvero tale, ma l'idea e questa.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			{
				"id": "colophon",
				"slug": "colophon",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "Colophon",
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-1",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-1s",
									"text": "Afterword is my personal site and small web workshop. It holds short updates, field notes, photographs, check-ins, media notes, older archive material, and longer writing without trying to behave like a single-purpose blog or a social profile.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-2",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-2s",
									"text": "The public site is now built with Astro and runs on Cloudflare Workers. EmDash is the CMS behind it, with the site content stored in D1 and local media stored in R2. Pages, posts, sections, forms, comments, menus, tags, categories, and much of the photo archive now live close to the site instead of being stitched together from far-away services on every request.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-3",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-3s",
									"text": "A small SvelteKit worker still lives at sync.afterword.blog. It is no longer the public site, but it remains useful as a backend sidecar for the messier integration work: Swarm/Foursquare check-ins, webhook receivers, music import jobs, and a few other sync tasks that are better handled by a custom service than by the front end itself.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-4",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-4s",
									"text": "Statuses come from Bluesky and AT Protocol. Check-ins are synced from Swarm into my own ATProto/PDS layer so they are not only trapped inside Swarm. The Astro site reads those records through faster local paths where it can, because I want the live parts to feel alive without making every visitor wait on a chain of distant APIs.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-5",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-5s",
									"text": "The gallery is intentionally more local now. Images from photography, field notes, and gallery-tagged posts are copied into my own media storage and rendered through the Astro site, with responsive gallery routes and lightbox views. That makes the photographs feel like part of this place rather than remote embeds wearing a local disguise.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-6",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-6s",
									"text": "Music and media are still a little more federated. Some of that material starts in places like Crucial Tracks, Album Whale, RSS feeds, or my PDS, then gets presented here as part of the broader site. The goal is not to hide the outside web, but to keep my own domain as the place where those signals gather.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-7",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-7s",
									"text": "There is also some standard.site and Bluesky syndication happening through EmDash and AT Protocol. That part is young, a little experimental, and exactly the kind of thing I like about this site: it lets writing begin here while still finding its way into other small-web and social-web spaces.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"_key": "colophon-current-8",
							"style": "normal",
							"markDefs": [],
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"_key": "colophon-current-8s",
									"text": "The larger point is still the same. I am not trying to build a product. I am trying to keep a personal web home that can hold the professional parts, the wandering and photography parts, the music-obsessive parts, the family-and-garden parts, and the ordinary notes that would otherwise disappear into platforms built for speed instead of memory.",
									"marks": []
								}
							]
						},
